  "selectedReplayRule": "Current required authorization precedes replay; exact authorized retries resolve the original accepted result using the selected logical identity and immutable actor/intent/source binding. Fresh mutable feasibility, clock selection and body preparation cannot replace that original result. Expected revision is concurrency precondition, not a new identity.",
  "productRules": [
    {
      "id": "D05-04",
      "doc": "m0-d05-application-inventory.md",
      "rule": "A SystemInstance's instance_kind is one of cloud_account, source_code_organization, identity_provider_tenant, saas_tenant, environment, or other; the other kind requires a description, and platform is required for every kind except environment and other."
    },
    {
      "id": "D05-05",
      "doc": "m0-d05-application-inventory.md",
      "rule": "An active SystemInstance's provider identifier is unique per tenant for the combination of instance kind, platform, and provider identifier, so same-named instances of different kinds or platforms do not collide."
    },
    {
      "id": "D22-01",
      "doc": "m0-d22-canonical-ownership.md",
      "rule": "Application and SystemInstance are owned solely by application inventory; access review campaigns reference an exact system instance, and a campaign's review inclusion neither creates nor owns the instance (ReviewedSystem is a legacy name, not a second entity)."
    }
  ],
  "decides": "Instance kind must be one of cloud_account, source_code_organization, identity_provider_tenant, saas_tenant, environment, or other; other requires a description, and platform is required for every kind except environment and other. An active instance's provider identifier is unique per tenant across (kind, platform, provider identifier), so same-named instances of different kinds or platforms do not collide. Access campaigns reference an exact instance and never create or own it.",
